[h1]Pop-Out Windows[/h1]
Put the game's windows on your other monitor – the main screen stays free for the world view and the map.

[list]
[*][b]Pop-out button[/b] in the title bar of every window – formation manager, message log, camera controls, unit status, sensor and doctrine windows: one click moves it to the other monitor, the same button there sends it back.
[*][b]Free-floating[/b] – only the windows show on that monitor, each with a thin frame; your desktop and other programs stay visible around them and take the clicks.
[*][b]Arrange them as you like[/b] – pop out several and drag them around; windows snap to each other and to the monitor's edges, and can be made larger than the game normally allows.
[*][b]Always in reach[/b] – while you're in the game they stay above other programs on that monitor.
[*][b]Remembered[/b] – popped-out windows open on the other monitor in the next mission too, where you left them.
[*][b]Wide resize corners[/b] on every window, on both screens: grab the end of an edge to resize diagonally.
[/list]

It is the game's own window over there – same look, dragging, resizing and clicks. Clicks on the other monitor never reach the world or the map, and the bottom-bar buttons keep working.

The map stays on the main screen – the game has its own options for putting the map or the world view on another monitor. A monitor the game uses for those is skipped automatically.

[h2]How to use[/h2]
Connect the second monitor before starting the game. In a mission, click the new button left of the [b]X[/b] in a window's title bar (a box with an arrow).

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[b]Anchor Chain[/b] is required: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3380210757]subscribe[/url] and follow its [url=https://seapower-modders.github.io/AnchorChain/install-anchor-chain.html]installation guide[/url] (one manual step: copy its preloader into the game folder).
A second monitor. Windows.

[h2]Settings[/h2]
[i]<Sea Power>\BepInEx\config\dev.sewerlabs.seapowerpopout.cfg[/i] – which monitor, UI scale over there, unlimited window size, see-through, always on top, snapping, wide resize corners.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
Sea Power 0.8.x. Works next to the game's own second-monitor map and detached world view. No game files are changed.

[h2]Problems?[/h2]
Please post the file [i]<Sea Power>\BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/i] with your report.

Source code (MIT): [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerPopOut]github.com/struckl/SeaPowerPopOut[/url]
